# Core Policy

- Follow `.specify/memory/constitution.md`; it outranks other project guidance.
- Ship production behavior only. Data may be fake only in explicit seeds or tests.
- Every visible action must work or be clearly disabled with an explanation.
  Never ship buttons or links that do nothing.
- Inspect before implementing. Reuse or extend existing components and modules;
  do not create duplicate implementations for stylistic preference.
- Use pnpm, strict TypeScript, and the constitution-approved stack.
- Never bypass RLS as a shortcut or expose privileged credentials to client code.
- Derive authorization from persisted memberships and assignments. Never hard-code
  a user's role or treat one global profile role as the full authority model.
- Keep student and private-club information non-public by default.
- The constitution committee consists solely of Mittansh Bhatia.
